<div class="page-head">
  <span class="label kicker">The guide, not the hero</span>
  <h1 class="h1 display balance">This isn't a ministry.<br>It's a dad, figuring it out.</h1>
</div>

<article class="article" style="padding-top:0;">
  <div class="article-body">
    <p>Somewhere along the way, most of us got handed a Bible that read like a rulebook — a behavior checklist we were already failing before we finished the first chapter. That's not what it is. It's the story of a God who transforms people through relationship, and a relationship changes how you actually live, not just what you claim to believe on a Sunday.</p>

    <p>That distinction is the whole reason this site exists.</p>

    <blockquote>It is for freedom that Christ has set us free; stand firm, then, and do not let yourselves be burdened again by a yoke of slavery. — Galatians 5:1</blockquote>

    <p>I'm not a professional theologian, and I'm not writing to people who already have this figured out. I'm a dad with two sons, working through Scripture out loud with them instead of just handing down conclusions — real study, honest disagreement, and free tools built to make the text accessible instead of academic.</p>

    <h2>If you're tired of a faith that lives in a box marked "Sunday," here's the plan</h2>

    <p><strong>Start with a chapter, not a system.</strong> Grab one of the free apps and actually open the text — Scripture Scout for digging into a passage, Groundwork for making prayer a daily habit instead of a once-a-week one.</p>

    <p><strong>Bring it home.</strong> Listen to the podcast — a father and his two sons working through a passage out loud, disagreements included.</p>

    <p><strong>Carry it into the week.</strong> Sermon Notes connect it back to Sunday. Field Notes connect it to whatever's actually in the headlines this week — because a relationship doesn't go quiet just because the news got loud.</p>

    <h2>Free. Always.</h2>

    <p>Not because none of this took real time to build — it did. But because a relationship that actually frees you shouldn't come with a paywall. Every app, every episode, every note stays free, always.</p>
  </div>

